    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense for August 12 is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 81.88. His leadoff positioning paired with a favorable matchup against Matthews (4.32 xERA) creates an ideal environment for run production. Crucially, we are tracking the slow delivery of Matthews, which provides a significant boost to the stolen base potential of **Gunnar Henderson**, a vital factor given the league's extreme scarcity of speed. Behind him, **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Drake Baldwin** (67.38) provide high-floor secondary options; **Sam Antonacci** benefits from a strong SP matchup (4.76 xERA) and prime lineup placement, while **Drake Baldwin** leverages a productive xwOBA profile against Thornton to outperform his base projection.\n\nOur most complex decision centered on the outfield, where **Kyle Tucker** (64.08) and **Andy Pages** (57.30) are currently slotted in pending official lineup confirmation. While **Kyle Tucker** remains a clear start, we are keeping a close eye on **Heliot Ramos** (45.65) and **Wade Meckler** (48.50). **Heliot Ramos** fell near the bottom of our start threshold due to a poor platoon dynamic against Miller, B, making him the most likely candidate to be swapped if we see late lineup shifts. **Nasim Nunez** (52.28) was the closest player to being benched; while his speed is valuable, he is hampered by a bottom-of-the-order assignment and David Peterson's elite ability to hold runners, which effectively cancels out the typical SB-driven upside we target for our MI slot. \n\nWe continue to monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg** and **Josh Jung**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our ability to rotate fresh legs into the infield. With **Jacob Wilson**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Lara** currently off the active card, our depth is thinner than we would prefer for a full Roto slate. While **Liam Hicks** (50.09) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (52.09) offer baseline value, their scores are somewhat suppressed by opponent SP skill and suboptimal platoon matchups. We are proceeding with the current configuration, but we remain ready to pivot if pre-game weather reports or finalized batting orders move our marginal starters below the 40-point floor.",
